<!--
If we want to be a bit more specific as to the elements we want to target. We can use a class. Elements that have the same class will be targeted.

Make the 3 paragraphs text red by using the class red in the <style> tag. A reminder on how to use class in a CSS declaration:

.red {
  color: red;
}

.red need to set color red
-->

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Hello World</title>
  <style>
    .red {
      color:red;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <p>Keep this paragraph black.</p>
  <p class="red">Make this paragraph Red.</p>
  <p class="red">Make this paragraph Red.</p>
  <p class="red">Make this paragraph Red.</p>
</body>
</html>